["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Find the food in shallow, calm water near a safe place to rest, and you have found the ducks.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view cross section of a marsh from a field on the left to deep water on the right. A field edge, then a muddy shore, then shallow water under 30 centimetres where a puddle duck tips up to feed, 75 percent. A band of cattails gives cover. Then deeper open water where a diver dives down to pondweed on the bottom, 80 percent.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A marsh, side view: who feeds where</text><path d=\"M0 120 L80 120 Q110 124 130 140 L170 150 L250 150 Q270 170 300 200 L400 210 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><path d=\"M110 136 L130 140 L170 150 L250 150 Q270 170 300 200 L400 210 L400 132 L110 132 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".55\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"104\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Field</text><line x1=\"176\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"176\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"183\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"183\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"197\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"197\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"204\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"204\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"211\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"211\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"218\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"218\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"225\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"225\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"232\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"232\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#6b7f3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><ellipse cx=\"206\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M300 206 q6 -20 0 -40 q-6 -20 2 -36\" stroke=\"#4f7d3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M330 206 q6 -20 0 -40 q-6 -20 2 -36\" stroke=\"#4f7d3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M360 206 q6 -20 0 -40 q-6 -20 2 -36\" stroke=\"#4f7d3a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><g transform=\"translate(136 128) rotate(70)\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g><path d=\"M134 116 l-6 -10 l8 2Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><g transform=\"translate(340 132) scale(0.6)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M10 -10 Q12 -18 16 -22 L22 -18 Q18 -12 18 -6 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-22\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -24 L35 -20 L24 -18 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(330 186)\"><ellipse rx=\"11\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"340\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"332\" y2=\"178\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"108\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dabblers: shallow</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">under 30 cm (75%)</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cattail</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Divers: deeper</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">open water (80%)</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pondweed</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mud edge, cattail, pondweed, open water</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Puddle ducks: shallow edges, under about 30 cm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Divers: deeper, open water <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: water depth and cover</summary><ul><li>Dabbling ducks feed best in water less than about 30 cm (12 in) deep; teal and pintail like the shallowest edges, 5 to 10 cm (70 to 75%).</li><li>Divers use bigger, deeper lakes and rivers and dive to the bottom for plants, snails and clams <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Cattail and bulrush bands give cover and nest sites <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Beaver ponds are duck ponds: shallow, full of food, sheltered (Tip).</li><li>Hunter meaning: on a big lake, puddle ducks sit in the shallow bays; divers raft off the points (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-cattail-marsh.jpg\" alt=\"Cattail marsh: cover and nest sites.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Cattail marsh: cover and nest sites. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Chris Light, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cat-tail_marsh_P6060104.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-pondweed.jpg\" alt=\"Floating pondweed: food for both groups.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Floating pondweed: food for both groups. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Christian Fischer, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PotamogetonNatans.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-beaver-lodge.jpg\" alt=\"Beaver pond: a duck pond.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Beaver pond: a duck pond. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Greenbilly, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beaver_pond_with_duck.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-kamloops-pond-farm.jpg\" alt=\"Pond, hay fields, cottonwoods near Kamloops.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Pond, hay fields, cottonwoods near Kamloops. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: cogdogblog, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Start_of_the_Mara_Trail,_Lac_Du_Bois_Grasslands_Protected_Area_(15721994786).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-lac-du-bois-potholes.jpg\" alt=\"Grassland potholes north of Kamloops.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Grassland potholes north of Kamloops. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Straitgate, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LacDuBoisBC.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-cattail-head.jpg\" alt=\"Cattail head: says \"marsh\" from 500 m.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Cattail head: says \"marsh\" from 500 m. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Terry.grignon, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Typha_latifolia_female_and_male_spikes.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Water, food and cover close together <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Small potholes hold puddle ducks; big lakes hold divers (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full habitat tour</summary><ul><li>Full tour with captions: <a href=\"#/s/habitat-ducks\">Habitat tour: ducks</a>.</li><li>The Interior rangeland holds about 250,000 ha of lakes and wetlands that support at least 300,000 breeding ducks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Forest country holds about 1,000,000 ha of lakes and wetlands with about 800,000 breeding waterfowl <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Most important waterfowl habitat in the Interior lies in the valleys and on mid elevation plateaus <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What ducks eat by season, 80 percent. Spring: insects and snails; hens need protein for eggs. Summer: ducklings eat insects; adults eat seeds and plants. Fall: marsh plant seeds, pondweed and waste grain in cut fields. Winter: grain fields; divers eat clams and snails. In October, find the food and you find the ducks, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What ducks eat, by season (80%)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"90\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spring</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bugs and snails:</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">hens need protein for eggs</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"98\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"98\" width=\"90\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d9a23a\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Summer</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Insects for ducklings:</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">adults eat seeds, plants</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"156\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"156\" width=\"90\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"189\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fall</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Seeds and grain:</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">marsh seeds, pondweed, cut fields</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"214\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"214\" width=\"90\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Winter</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grain and seeds:</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"257\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">divers add clams, snails</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">October: find the food, find the ducks (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Fall: marsh seeds, pondweed, waste grain <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Divers add snails, clams and insects <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: food in your areas</summary><ul><li>Fall foods: seeds of marsh plants, pondweed, waste grain in cut fields <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Mallards and pintails feed in harvested grain fields at dawn and dusk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Shovelers sieve tiny animals with their comb edged bill <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Laying hens need protein: snails and insects in spring <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Fraser delta waterfowl need food from September to April, much of it on farm fields <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: a cut grain field next to a pond is a mallard magnet. Ask the farmer (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of where ducks are by elevation each month, general pattern, 60 percent. January and February: 0 to 700 metres. March: up to 1,000. April: up to 1,500. May to August: 300 to 1,500 metres on breeding wetlands. September and October: 0 to 1,500. November: 0 to 1,000. December: 0 to 700. Freeze up pushes them low, below about 700 metres.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Duck elevations by month (60%)</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"156.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"84.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text><rect x=\"75\" y=\"156.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"84.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"86\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">F</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"120.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"120.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">M</text><rect x=\"133\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"180.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><rect x=\"162\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"144.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"173\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">M</text><rect x=\"191\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"144.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"144.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"231\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text><rect x=\"249\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"144.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"180.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"289\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">S</text><rect x=\"307\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"180.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text><rect x=\"336\" y=\"120.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"120.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"347\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">N</text><rect x=\"365\" y=\"156.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"84.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"376\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"240.0\" x2=\"394\" y2=\"240.0\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"245.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">0</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"180.0\" x2=\"394\" y2=\"180.0\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"185.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">500</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"394\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"125.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">1000</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"394\" y2=\"60.0\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"65.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">1500</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Freeze up pushes them low: below 700 m</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Summer: 300 to 1,500 m wetlands <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Winter: low valley water under about 700 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the pattern</summary><ul><li>Breeding: Interior wetlands and potholes from about 300 to 1,500 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Lesser scaup, canvasback and redhead breed on plateau lakes at 500 to 1,500 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Plateau lakes start to freeze in October; birds pack onto valley water in November (60 to 65%).</li><li>Winter: open water from sea level to about 700 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>These are general bands from the app migration data, not counts (55 to 65%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 618\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Duck water near Kamloops. Open, confirmed on official pages, 99 percent: Lac du Bois Grasslands potholes north of the city line, Deep Lake walk in only. Roche Lake Park south of Kamloops, 7 lakes, 2 with gravel roads. Bonaparte Park, by logging roads up Jamieson Creek or float plane. Closed to shooting: Tranquille marsh, a No Shooting or Hunting Area; McQueen, Griffin and Isobel Lakes within 1 kilometre; and farther out Logan Lake, Salmon Arm bay, Blind Bay, Mara Lake and the Sicamous end of Shuswap Lake. North and South Thompson rivers: no official spot, Crown land or written permission only.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"618\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">Open: confirmed on an official page (99%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"34\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"62.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><path d=\"M26.9 64.0 l4.8 4.8 l9.5 -10.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Lac du Bois potholes</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">North of the city line. Deep Lake: walk in.</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"98\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"136.0\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><path d=\"M26.9 137.5 l4.8 4.8 l9.5 -10.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Roche Lake Park</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">South of Kamloops. 7 lakes, 2 with gravel</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"159\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">roads.</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"181\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"219.0\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><path d=\"M26.9 220.5 l4.8 4.8 l9.5 -10.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Bonaparte Park</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Logging roads up Jamieson Creek, or float</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">plane.</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Closed to shooting</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"292\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8e9e5\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"320.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><path d=\"M28.9 315.4 l10.2 10.2 M39.1 315.4 l-10.2 10.2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Tranquille marsh</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"334\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">No Shooting or Hunting Area.</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"356\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8e9e5\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"384.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><path d=\"M28.9 379.4 l10.2 10.2 M39.1 379.4 l-10.2 10.2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"378\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">McQueen, Griffin, Isobel</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"398\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">No shooting within 1 km.</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"420\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8e9e5\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"458.0\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><path d=\"M28.9 452.9 l10.2 10.2 M39.1 452.9 l-10.2 10.2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"442\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Farther out</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"462\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Logan Lake, Salmon Arm bay, Blind Bay,</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"481\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Mara Lake, Sicamous end.</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"521\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2c5d86\">Rivers</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"531\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eaf0f6\" stroke=\"#2c5d86\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"569.0\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2c5d86\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"575\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"553\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">North and South Thompson</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"573\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">No official spot. Crown land or permission</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"592\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">only.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Lac du Bois potholes, Roche Lake, Bonaparte (99%, see the local plan).</li><li>Tranquille marsh is closed to shooting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where ducks are around your base</summary><ul><li>Mallard and gadwall breed in clusters in the Thompson and Nicola wetlands, mostly below 500 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Wigeon concentrate in the Thompson drainage <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Barrow's goldeneye: core range is the dry Interior parkland, your country <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Bufflehead are common in the lower Thompson drainage <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>The South Thompson River is an Important Bird Area and holds wintering ducks on open water <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Legal water, closures and access are in the local plan, not repeated here: <a href=\"#/s/local-heffley/13\">Local plan: ducks, legal water</a> and <a href=\"#/s/local-heffley/5\">Where you cannot shoot</a>.</li><li>District No. 3 dates and limits: <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/10\">Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 523\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Duck water near Mission. Read the legal text before you set up. Fraser River in bylaw Area B: shotgun with shot only while hunting, 99 percent. Hatzic Lake and Harrison Bay: firearms using shot only, 98 percent. Pitt Addington Marsh: some areas on certain days, posted on site, 80 percent, special licence applies. Matsqui Island is Indian Reserve 3, reserve land, ask the band first, 95 percent. Lhá:lt Harrison Chehalis and Bert Brink Wildlife Management Areas: hunting status VERIFY. Parts of Hatzic Slough, Hatzic Prairie and Deroche: No Shooting areas, 98 percent. Boundary Bay Wildlife Management Area: closed to snipe hunting, 99 percent.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"523\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\">Read the legal text before you set up</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"60.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><path d=\"M26.9 62.0 l4.8 4.8 l9.5 -10.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Fraser, bylaw Area B</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Shotgun with shot only, while hunting (99%).</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"96\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"124.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><path d=\"M26.9 126.0 l4.8 4.8 l9.5 -10.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Hatzic Lake, Harrison Bay</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Firearms using shot only (98%).</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"160\" width=\"380\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eaf0f6\" stroke=\"#2c5d86\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"198.0\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2c5d86\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Pitt Addington Marsh</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Some areas, some days, posted on site</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"221\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">(80%). Special licence.</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"243\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eaf0f6\" stroke=\"#2c5d86\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"271.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2c5d86\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"277.5\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Matsqui Island</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">I.R. 3, reserve land. Ask the band first (95%).</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"307\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eaf0f6\" stroke=\"#2c5d86\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"335.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2c5d86\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"341.5\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">?</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"329\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Harrison Chehalis, Bert Brink WMAs</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"349\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Hunting status: VERIFY.</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"371\" width=\"380\" height=\"77\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8e9e5\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"409.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><path d=\"M28.9 404.4 l10.2 10.2 M39.1 404.4 l-10.2 10.2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"393\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Parts of Hatzic Slough, Prairie,</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"413\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Deroche</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"433\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">No Shooting areas (98%).</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"455\" width=\"380\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8e9e5\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"483.5\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><path d=\"M28.9 478.4 l10.2 10.2 M39.1 478.4 l-10.2 10.2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"477\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Boundary Bay WMA</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"497\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Closed to snipe hunting (99%).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Wood duck country: the lower Fraser Valley <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Wintering ducks on the delta, fields and sloughs <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the Fraser Valley duck picture</summary><ul><li>The lower Fraser Valley is the centre of wood duck abundance in BC <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Blue winged teal have a breeding cluster in the lower Fraser Valley <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Wintering areas: Fraser delta fields and sloughs, Pitt Addington Marsh, Harrison Chehalis, Boundary Bay (65 to 90%).</li><li>Every spot has its own rules, a special area licence and bylaws: <a href=\"#/s/local-mission/2\">Local plan: Mission</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/28\">Rule Book, near Mission</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-osoyoos-wetland.jpg\" alt=\"Haynes Point wetland, Osoyoos Lake: reeds and calm water.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Haynes Point wetland, Osoyoos Lake: reeds and calm water. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: B&amp;B-Traveller, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haynes_Point_Wetland_Project,_Osoyoos_Lake,_BC,_Canada_-_panoramio.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Mallards, gadwall and wigeon on valley wetlands <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Vaseux Lake is a sanctuary: no hunting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: on your quail trip</summary><ul><li>Okanagan wetlands hold breeding mallard and gadwall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Vaseux Lake is an Important Bird Area and a migratory bird sanctuary: no hunting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Some Okanagan waters and the Osoyoos Oxbows have closures: read <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Rule Book: Region 8</a> before you load a gun.</li><li>District No. 8 dates and limits: <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/15\">Rule Book</a>.</li><li>Tip: a quail trip in November can include an evening duck sit, if you carry steel shot only on that hunt (law on lead in <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/18\">Methods</a>).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Use the Hunt Map in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 1. A phone map with ponds. The Duck staging and winter waters layer outlines the big lake in orange, and the Wetlands layer outlines a small marsh in green dashes. Caption: turn on the Duck waters and Wetlands layers.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunt Map 1: find the water</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"34\" width=\"280\" height=\"214\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8eadf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M64 140 Q140 120 200 150 T336 140\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M150 90 Q190 70 230 92 Q250 120 210 130 Q160 132 150 90Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M250 180 