troke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"78\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"76.0\" y=\"48.0\" width=\"56.7\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f8f4a\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"104.347\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#246b38\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Park?</text>\n<line x1=\"96\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"96\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"155\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"68.0\" y=\"98.0\" width=\"70.8\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"103.409\" y=\"117\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">MU line</text>\n<line x1=\"240\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"216.965\" y2=\"225\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"222\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"150.0\" y=\"212.0\" width=\"67.0\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#b5473a\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"183.483\" y=\"231\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#9b3328\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Private</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Add Private land, Parks, MU lines</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Add Private land, Parks and MU lines.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 3. The Sun and shade tool shows where the sun will be. The hide sits on the west shore so the morning sun is behind it and in the eyes of incoming ducks, a tip. Caption: sun and shade, sun behind your hide.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunt Map 3: sun and slope</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"34\" width=\"280\" height=\"214\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8eadf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M64 140 Q140 120 200 150 T336 140\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M150 90 Q190 70 230 92 Q250 120 210 130 Q160 132 150 90Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M250 180 Q280 168 310 186 Q300 210 268 206 Q246 200 250 180Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M80 190 Q110 178 130 196 Q120 214 92 210Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".6\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"70\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#f2b632\"/><line x1=\"282\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"241.4128053298139\" y2=\"97.41126701617597\" stroke=\"#d9a23a\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"236.0,100.0 248.5,100.7 243.3,89.8\" fill=\"#d9a23a\"/><rect x=\"116\" y=\"96\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6b6f4a\"/><text x=\"129\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hide</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sun</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sun and shade: sun behind your hide</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Use Sun and shade: sun behind your hide.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 4. The What can I see from here tool, from a knoll beside the lake, shades the water you can see. Use it to pick a place to glass the ducks before the hunt. Caption: what can I see from here, a spotting knoll.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunt Map 4: glass it first</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"34\" width=\"280\" height=\"214\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8eadf\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M64 140 Q140 120 200 150 T336 140\" stroke=\"#c9c9b9\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M150 90 Q190 70 230 92 Q250 120 210 130 Q160 132 150 90Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M250 180 Q280 168 310 186 Q300 210 268 206 Q246 200 250 180Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M80 190 Q110 178 130 196 Q120 214 92 210Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".6\"/><path d=\"M100 70 L250 60 L250 140 L100 150Z\" fill=\"#f2b632\" opacity=\".3\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"110\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Knoll</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Seen from the knoll</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What can I see from here: a spotting knoll</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Use What can I see from here to pick a glassing knoll.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Layers find the water; land status says if you can hunt it (Tip).</li><li>Open the <a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every layer and tool, and how to use it for ducks</summary><ul><li>Layer \"Duck staging and winter waters\": valley lakes and wetlands of 20 ha or more where ducks stop in fall and spring, plus low open water in winter (app layer guide).</li><li>Layer \"Wetlands\": marshes, swamps and bogs from the Freshwater Atlas. Small potholes for puddle ducks (app layer guide).</li><li>Land status: Private land, Parks and protected areas, Reserves, MU (Management Unit) lines and numbers. A pond in private land needs permission <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Terrain tools: Slope steepness (find a gentle walk in for a heavy decoy bag), Slope direction (aspect: south facing shores warm and open first), What can I see from here (a knoll to glass the water from), Sun and shade (put the rising sun behind you, in the ducks' eyes) (all Tips).</li><li>Scent cone and wind: check which shore will have the wind at your back or side for the landing (Tip).</li><li>Insights on a spot shows the month band for ducks from the app migration data (55 to 65%).</li><li>Field task: drop a waypoint on each pond you scout, with a note of what you saw.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"Shallow for dabblers, deep for divers\"</td><td>Under about 30 cm vs open water (75 to 80%)</td></tr><tr><td>\"Food, water, rest within a short flight\"</td><td>Where ducks settle <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>700 m</td><td>Winter ducks below this <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Wood ducks: Mission. Barrow's: Kamloops.\"</td><td>Your bases <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Layers find it, land status clears it\"</td><td>Hunt Map (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"Find the food and you have found the ducks.\"</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Beaver pond, duck pond.\" (Tip)</li><li>\"When the high lakes lock, hunt the river.\" Freeze up pushes ducks to valley water <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Main source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Habitat, food</td><td>Ducks Unlimited, university extension</td></tr><tr><td>Where in BC</td><td>BC Breeding Bird Atlas</td></tr><tr><td>Map layers</td><td>App layer guide and migration data</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source, with date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://extension.umd.edu/sites/extension.umd.edu/files/2021-03/FS610_WMgtDabDuck.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">University of Maryland Extension, managing wetlands for dabbling ducks</a> and <a href=\"https://cnhp.colostate.edu/download/documents/cwic_docs/CPWSpeciesProfiles/CPWProfiles_Dabbling%20Ducks.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Colorado species profile, dabbling ducks</a>: under 30 cm, 10 to 30 cm. Search preview 2026-10-11 (70 to 75%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/conservation/international-conservation-plan/bc-intermountain\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, BC Intermountain</a>: habitat areas and duck numbers. Read directly 2026-10-11 (70 to 75%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.birdatlas.bc.ca/accounts/speciesaccount.jsp?lang=en&amp;sp=MALL\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Breeding Bird Atlas</a>: where each duck breeds. Checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.ca/assets/2021/10/waterfowl-ID-guide-2020-EN-reader-spreads.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited Canada ID guide</a>: foods. Checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/understanding-waterfowl-duck-digestion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, duck digestion</a>: shoveler bill, hen protein. Read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>App data: data/migration.json (ducks, months and named waters, checked 2026-10-03, 55 to 90%) and the Hunt Map layer guide.</li><li>Local legal water and closures: the app local plans and Rule Book (99% where quoted there).</li></ul></details>"]